This directory is NOT covered by the repository's Business Source License.

`trekkers.png` and `emotes.png` are derived from Kenney asset packs released under
Creative Commons CC0 1.0 Universal (https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/) —
a public-domain dedication. Repacking them into sheets does not create any new
restriction, and CC0 cannot be withdrawn, so these two files remain in the public domain:

    No attribution required.  Commercial use fine.  No copyleft.  No share-alike.

Take them and use them for anything. The repository's licence (../LICENSE) applies to the
game code that draws them, not to the art itself.

We credit Kenney anyway, because Kenney asks nicely and it costs nothing:

    Player sprites by Kenney — https://kenney.nl

Full provenance (pack names and versions, download URLs, SHA-256 of the original zips,
exactly which frames were used and what was changed) is in CREDITS.md. `build-sheets.py`
rebuilds both sheets from the upstream zips and produces byte-identical output, which is
how you can verify these files contain nothing but the CC0 frames listed there.

Upstream licence texts, verbatim from inside the packs, plus the full CC0 1.0 legal code:

    licenses/kenney_new-platformer-pack_License.txt
    licenses/kenney_emotes-pack_License.txt
    licenses/CC0-1.0.txt

`build-sheets.py` is our own code and is covered by ../LICENSE.
